        explanation: "- Self-service environments are the capability teams ask for most: a real place to run a branch, with data, a URL and an expiry\n- Give every ephemeral environment a time to live. Without expiry, cost grows monotonically and the cluster fills with abandoned namespaces\n- Seed data deliberately: synthetic or anonymised. Copying production data into ephemeral environments is the most common way a platform creates a compliance incident\n- Workload identity replaces static credentials: OIDC federation lets a pipeline or pod assume a cloud role without a stored key, so there is no secret to leak or rotate\n- Secrets belong in a manager (Vault, cloud secret managers) and are projected into workloads by an operator. Encrypted-in-Git is still a copy that leaves with anyone who clones the repository\n- Policy as code enforces the standards at admission: Kyverno and Gatekeeper evaluate every resource against rules — no root containers, resource limits required, approved registries only, tags present\n- Run policy in audit mode first, publish the violations per team, fix the paved road so compliance is automatic, and only then enforce\n- Verify provenance before running code: signed images (cosign), an SBOM per build, and an admission rule rejecting unsigned or unscanned artefacts\n- Secure by default is a platform attribute, not a review step: if the golden path produces a compliant service without the team thinking about it, security scales with adoption",
        keyPoints: [
          { tone: "key", title: "Every environment needs a TTL", text: "Expiry is what keeps self-service affordable. Make extension easy and deletion automatic." },
          { tone: "key", title: "Replace keys with identity", text: "OIDC-federated workload identity removes the long-lived cloud credential entirely, which removes the leak and the rotation problem." },
          { tone: "key", title: "Audit before enforce", text: "A policy switched straight to enforce breaks deploys and burns trust. Publish violations, fix the templates, then enforce." },
          { tone: "tip", title: "Seed synthetic data", text: "A realistic fake dataset is a platform capability; it makes ephemeral environments useful without copying personal data." },
          { tone: "tip", title: "Policy exemptions need an owner and an expiry", text: "Permanent, unattributed exceptions are how policy quietly stops meaning anything." },
          { tone: "warning", title: "Encrypted secrets in Git are still distributed secrets", text: "Anyone who can clone the repository holds the ciphertext forever; rotation cannot recall it." },
          { tone: "warning", title: "Do not let security gates sit outside the paved road", text: "If scanning and signing are extra steps a team must remember, coverage will track memory rather than policy." },
        ],
        example: "- A pull request labelled preview gets a namespace, seeded data and a URL, expiring in 72 hours\n- A pipeline assumes a cloud role through OIDC, so no cloud key exists in CI secrets\n- Kyverno in audit mode reports 212 violations; after template fixes, 9 remain and enforcement begins\n- An unsigned image is rejected at admission rather than discovered in a quarterly review\n- A policy exemption carries an owner and a 30-day expiry, so it cannot become permanent by default",
        code: "# 1. Enforce standards at admission — audit first, then enforce.\napiVersion: kyverno.io/v1\nkind: ClusterPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: platform-baseline\n  annotations: { policies.kyverno.io/description: 'Paved-road baseline for all workloads.' }\nspec:\n  validationFailureAction: Audit        # flip to Enforce once violations are near zero\n  background: true\n  rules:\n    - name: require-resource-limits\n      match: { any: [{ resources: { kinds: [Pod] } }] }\n      validate:\n        message: 'Every container needs CPU and memory limits.'\n        pattern:\n          spec:\n            containers:\n              - resources: { limits: { memory: '?*', cpu: '?*' } }\n    - name: approved-registries-only\n      match: { any: [{ resources: { kinds: [Pod] } }] }\n      validate:\n        message: 'Images must come from the internal registry.'\n        pattern:\n          spec:\n            containers:\n              - image: 'registry.acme.internal/*'\n    - name: verify-image-signature\n      match: { any: [{ resources: { kinds: [Pod] } }] }\n      verifyImages:\n        - imageReferences: ['registry.acme.internal/*']\n          attestors:\n            - entries: [{ keyless: { issuer: 'https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com', subject: 'https://github.com/acme/*' } }]\n\n# 2. Ephemeral environment with an expiry the platform enforces.\napiVersion: platform.acme.internal/v1alpha1\nkind: Environment\nmetadata: { name: pr-4821, namespace: team-orders }\nspec:\n  source: { repo: orders-api, ref: pr-4821 }\n  dataset: synthetic-small            # never a production copy\n  ttl: 72h                            # reclaimed automatically\n  expose: { public: false }\n\n# 3. No long-lived cloud keys: the pipeline federates an identity instead.\n# .github/workflows/deploy.yml\n# permissions: { id-token: write, contents: read }\n# - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n#   with: { role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/deploy-orders, aws-region: ap-south-1 }",
