        explanation: "- Measure outcomes for the teams using the platform: CNCF groups them as user satisfaction and productivity, organisational efficiency, and product delivery performance\n- Compare delivery metrics on and off the paved road. A platform that helps should show shorter lead times and lower change fail rates for the teams that adopted it\n- Time to first deploy for a brand-new service is the clearest onboarding measure, and the one new joiners feel immediately\n- Track support load per capability. A capability generating constant questions has a leaky abstraction or missing documentation, and that is a roadmap item\n- Survey deliberately and sparingly: a short quarterly survey with a free-text 'what slowed you down?' field produces more signal than a dashboard of usage counts\n- Publish a platform status and roadmap: capability status (experimental, beta, GA, deprecated), what is coming, what is being retired and when\n- Deprecate like a product: announce, provide migration tooling and a window, help the last few teams, then remove. Silent removals destroy the trust that adoption depends on\n- Staff for product work, not queue work: if the team spends most of its time on requests, self-service is missing somewhere, and the fix is a capability rather than more staff\n- Keep an enablement loop: office hours, pairing with a team through an onboarding, and an internal channel where the platform team answers in public so answers become documentation",
