    project: "Design and build the thinnest viable platform for an organisation you know. Start with research: interview three teams and write down every step between 'we need a new service' and 'it serves production traffic', with the time each takes. Publish a capability inventory naming owner, status and how each capability is consumed. Then build two capabilities properly. First, a golden-path template that generates a service with a working pipeline, container build, deployment manifests, a dashboard and a catalog-info.yaml with a required owner — asking at most three questions, recording its template version, and covered by a daily CI job that scaffolds it and asserts the result serves traffic. Second, one self-service infrastructure resource behind a platform API: a composite resource with intent-level fields, a non-negotiable security setting, honest status reporting and an explicit deletion policy per environment. Wrap both in paved-road security: OIDC workload identity instead of stored cloud keys, an admission policy run in audit mode until the templates satisfy it, and signed images verified before they run. Finally, publish the measurement set — time to first deploy, fulfilment latency, voluntary adoption, on-path versus off-path delivery metrics and support load by capability — and review it after a month against the times you recorded in the interviews.",
